/// Stores a word through the first argument and returns that argument.
///
/// Ghidra types the body as `void` and its callers immediately store the result
/// of the call in a word, so the real function returns `r3`. The callers only
/// ever use it to materialise a value on the stack.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_802537d0` at `0x802537d0` (8 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/802537d0_FUN_802537d0.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `dst`: writable word.
/// - `value`: word to store.
///
/// # Returns
/// `dst`.
///
/// # Side effects
/// One word store.
///
/// # Safety
/// `dst` must be writable for four bytes.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - the store is literal; the return value is restored from the call
/// sites (`*FUN_802537d0(...)`), because the export shows `void`.
pub unsafe fn fn_802537d0(dst: usize, value: u32) -> usize {
    write_u32(dst, value);
    dst
}

/// The same "store and return the pointer" leaf as [`fn_802537d0`], used by the
/// `0x80258C80` getter.
