// ===========================================================================
// 0x80250CB0..0x8025EEB0 -- the render-node object behind the transform node
//                            (Wave 91, manual)

// ===========================================================================
//
// **What lives here.** Eight small clusters of the `0x80250000` bucket. They all
// operate on the same two-level shape the `0x802539xx` section above already
// documents: an API function receives a *holder* whose first word is the object
// pointer, and every body starts with `object = *holder`. The object itself is
// the rendering node whose 3x4 matrix sits at `+0x30`, whose flag word sits at
// `+0x70` (bit `0x10` "no rotation", bit `0x20` "use the `+0xAC` quad", bit
// `0x40`/`0x80` "matrix path already taken") and whose float fields run from
// `+0xAC` to `+0xF0`.
//
// - **Cluster 1 (`0x80250CB0..0x80250DF0`)** -- matrix initialisation. Two
//   bodies test a per-shape helper and identity-initialise the caller's matrix
//   when it succeeded; four leaves return fixed data addresses; the last body
//   writes three floats and sets one of three flag patterns.
// - **Cluster 2 (`0x802537E0..0x802543D0`)** -- the node's default state and
//   the six dispatch wrappers that turn its float fields into matrix kernels.
//   `0x80253830` is the reset writer (every `+0x74..+0x108` field), `0x802537E0`
//   is its only caller, and the six wrappers pick a `0x801C0Fxx`/`0x801C12xx`
//   kernel from the flag word.
// - **Cluster 3 (`0x80258BD0..0x80258C80`)** -- three getters over two strided
//   arrays: `0x20` records of `0x10C` bytes at `+0xF8` and `0x20` records of
//   `0x30` bytes at `+0x2278`.
// - **Cluster 4 (`0x80259110`, `0x80259280`, `0x802592E0`)** -- event forwards:
//   fetch the current slot, run the view pass, report one event on the object's
//   own vtable.
// - **Cluster 5 (`0x80259FC0`, `0x8025A050`)** -- the two sort comparators: same
//   bit trick, different key byte and vtable slot.
// - **Cluster 6 (`0x8025A290`, `0x8025BE30`, `0x8025C8E0`, `0x8025C960`,
//   `0x8025EEB0`)** -- five unrelated leaves: a positive-size release, the
//   five-slot virtual sweep, the lazy boolean setter, the child cursor builder
//   and the TV-format resource selector.
//
// **Why it matters.** The matrix kernels are the only place where the node's
// float layout is consumed: `+0xAC..+0xB8` is the position/scale quad, `+0xBC..
// +0xC8` a second quad, `+0xCC..+0xD8` a third, and `+0xDC..+0xF0` the pair used
// by `0x80254340`. No SDK symbol survives for any of them, so every name is
// `fn_<address>` and every role below is either `// observed:` or `// inferred:`.
//
// **Dependencies.** `crate::platform` only, plus the [`sda`]/[`sda2`] helpers and
// the local [`read_u64`]. The five float-argument kernels are reached through
// host-side `extern "C"` trampolines because the platform `callN` helpers only
// move general-purpose registers; the same convention is used by
// `src/audio/ax.rs` for the FPR-argument math helpers.
/// `r2-0x4990`: first 4-byte data constant of the render-node class.
///
/// Written into `+0x74`, `+0x78`, `+0x80`, the `+0x88`..`+0xA4` block, `+0xBC`,
/// `+0xDC`, `+0xE0` and `+0xEC`, and into the last-but-one matrix word by
/// [`fn_802542c0`]. `// unknown:` the value; only "a constant shared by every
/// node" is proven.
const SDA2_RENDER_A: isize = -0x4990;
/// `r2-0x498C`: second data constant, written to `+0x7C` only.
const SDA2_RENDER_B: isize = -0x498c;
/// `r2-0x4988`: third data constant, written to `+0x84`, `+0xF0` and the last
/// matrix word of [`fn_802542c0`].
const SDA2_RENDER_C: isize = -0x4988;
/// `r2-0x4984`: fourth data constant, written to `+0xAC`.
const SDA2_RENDER_D: isize = -0x4984;
/// `r2-0x4980`: fifth data constant, written to `+0xB0`.
const SDA2_RENDER_E: isize = -0x4980;
/// `r2-0x497C`: sixth data constant, written to `+0xB4`.
const SDA2_RENDER_F: isize = -0x497c;
/// `r2-0x4978`: seventh data constant, written to `+0xB8`.
const SDA2_RENDER_G: isize = -0x4978;
/// `r2-0x4974`: eighth data constant, written to `+0xCC`..`+0xD8`.
const SDA2_RENDER_H: isize = -0x4974;
/// `r2-0x4970`: the 8-byte constant subtracted from the `0x4330_0000`-biased
/// doubles in [`fn_80253830`]. `0x4330000000000000` is `2^52`, so the idiom is
