// 1. The model-instance loaders `0x80251E50`..`0x80252440`. They walk the
//    four-byte tag array built by the resource loader (a `0x01` tag byte ends
//    the walk), resolve each tag through the three table lookups
//    `0x8023B2A0`/`0x8023B950`/`0x8023B800`, and hand a five-word key to
//    `0x80251930` and then to the packet emitter `0x8024E180`.
// 2. The transform kernels `0x80254910`..`0x80256F90`. Three dispatch wrappers
//    select one of seven kernels from the gather-format field `(word >> 1) & 7`
//    in six contiguous seven-entry tables at `0x802F8EF0`..`0x802F8F98`, three
//    "emit one node" bodies write twelve floats and three vertex words, and
//    four small matrix builders rotate a two-column matrix by an angle.
// 3. The vertex-format object `0x8025A380`..`0x8025C250`: an allocator, a
//    three-way matrix picker, a five-slot detach sweep, a slot getter, and the
//    destructor. Its five owned slots live at `+0x124`..`+0x134`, its vertex
//    arrays at `+0xEC`/`+0xF4`, and its layer geometry at `+0x101`/`+0x102`.
// 4. Two `0x288C`-header render objects (`0x802589E0`, `0x802593E0`) whose
//    header publishes the `0x8034E828`/`0x8034E858` vtables, plus the four
//    node-level entries `0x80257E60`, `0x80259190`, `0x8025B420` and
//    `0x8025EFB0`.
//
// **`0x802DCDxx` is a register-handoff entry, not a normal callee.** The
// entries used here are four bytes wide in `functions.tsv` yet their Ghidra
// bodies store between seven and fourteen registers, so the recorded size is
// not a real function size. Waves 92 and 96 already model these entries as
// opaque 64-bit-returning calls; this pass keeps that convention, names the
// half it reads at every call site, and marks the halves `// unknown:` where
// the export gives no more than `(ulonglong)uVarN >> 0x20`.
//
// **Dependencies.** `crate::platform` plus the local [`sda`]/[`sda2`] and the
// three translated bodies this pass calls back into
// ([`fn_80251e50`], [`fn_802593e0`], [`fn_8025f2b0`]).
