// ===========================================================================
// 0x801B3010..0x801BBA30 -- the SI serial-interface layer, the play-time
//                            state machine and its SRAM mirror (Wave 98)

// ===========================================================================
//
// **What lives here.** The middle of the `0x801B0000` bucket: the serial
// interface (`/dev/net/kd` and `/dev/si`) that carries the boot-time device
// probe, the play-time expiry state machine and its SRAM mirror, and the
// descriptor/queue helpers those paths share. Wave 86 translated the outer
// boot sequence and Wave 93 the EXI channel layer; the bodies below are the SI
// side of the same code plus the two gaps those waves left in the play-time
// cluster.
//
// **The SI state block.**
// - `0x8038F7D0`: four `0x20`-byte transfer descriptors. `+0x00` is the
//   `0x802DCD5C` pair (channel, device), `+0x08` the byte count, `+0x0C` the
//   buffer, `+0x10` the rate, `+0x14` the completion callback and `+0x18` the
//   64-bit deadline. `0xFFFFFFFF` in the first word means "free".
// - `0x8038F850` / `0x8038F870`: four 64-bit start and last-completion stamps.
// - `0x8038F9A0`: four command words; `0x8038F9B0`: four callbacks per
//   channel; `0x8038F9F0`: the `u16` scan-result table, decoded through the
//   `u16` table at `0x8038FA68`.
// - `0x8033FF90` is the active channel (`-1` idle), `0x8033FF94` the control
//   word, `0x8033FF98`/`0x8033FF9C` the pending length and buffer,
//   `0x8033FFA0` the completion callback and `0x8033FFA8` four words of
//   per-channel state.
//
// **The register handoffs.** `0x802DCD4C`..`0x802DCD74` are four-byte entries
// that hand back the caller's register pair; `call_u64` reads both halves. As
// in waves 92/96/97 every body names the half it uses and cites the export
// line. `0x802DCD98`, `0x802DCDA8`, `0x802DCDB0`, `0x802DCDB8`,
// `0x802DCDBC` and `0x802DCDC0` publish the result of the entry they close.
//
// **Dependencies.** `crate::platform`, the local [`sda`]/[`sda2`] helpers, the
// EXI constants and [`exi_control`]/[`exi_reg`] from Wave 93, and
// [`get_time`]/[`read_time_base`].
/// `0x800000F8`: MEM1 bus clock in Hz. `>> 2` is the time-base tick rate the
/// SI timeouts are expressed in.
const W98_BUS_CLOCK: usize = 0x8000_00f8;
/// `0x8038F7D0`: four `0x20`-byte SI transfer descriptors.
const W98_SI_DESC: usize = 0x8038_f7d0;
/// Byte stride between [`W98_SI_DESC`] entries.
const W98_SI_DESC_STRIDE: usize = 0x20;
/// `0x8038F850`: four 64-bit transfer start stamps.
const W98_SI_START: usize = 0x8038_f850;
/// `0x8038F870`: four 64-bit last-completion stamps.
const W98_SI_LAST: usize = 0x8038_f870;
/// `0x8038F9A0`: one command word per channel.
const W98_SI_CMD: usize = 0x8038_f9a0;
/// `0x8038F9B0`: four completion callbacks per channel (`0x10` bytes each).
const W98_SI_CALLBACK: usize = 0x8038_f9b0;
/// `0x8038F9F0`: `u16` scan-result table, one entry per decoded bit.
const W98_SI_SCAN: usize = 0x8038_f9f0;
/// `0x8038FA68`: `u16` values written into [`W98_SI_SCAN`].
const W98_SI_SCAN_VALUE: usize = 0x8038_fa68;
/// `0x8033FF90`: active SI channel, `-1` when idle.
const W98_SI_INDEX: usize = 0x8033_ff90;
/// `0x8033FF94`: SI control word (timeout and enable bits).
const W98_SI_CONTROL: usize = 0x8033_ff94;
/// `0x8033FF98`: pending transfer length.
const W98_SI_LENGTH: usize = 0x8033_ff98;
/// `0x8033FF9C`: pending transfer buffer.
const W98_SI_BUFFER: usize = 0x8033_ff9c;
/// `0x8033FFA0`: pending completion callback.
const W98_SI_CALLBACK_PTR: usize = 0x8033_ffa0;
/// `0x8033FFA8`: four words of per-channel state.
const W98_SI_STATE: usize = 0x8033_ffa8;
/// `0x800030C0`: four per-channel progress counters.
const W98_SI_COUNTER: usize = 0x8000_30c0;
