/// `0x801B64D0` and mode `5` reads a 32-bit code word. Whatever the mode
/// produced is then mapped to a font base: a zero encoding index, or a code
/// below `0x80` while `sda(-0x4FC4)` is set, sends the code through
/// `0x801B65C0`, and a successful remap switches the base from
/// `sda(-0x4FBC)` to `sda(-0x4FC0)` and passes flag `1` to the glyph
/// allocator `0x801AFDB0`.
