/// - Ghidra: `FUN_801b06a0` at `0x801b06a0` (436 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/801b06a0_FUN_801b06a0.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `mode`: encoding selector; also the first argument of `0x801AFDB0` when
///   the code point stayed in the raw single-byte path (modes `0`/`1`).
/// - `text`: pointer to the first byte of the character.
/// - `out_font`: receives the font base (`sda(-0x4FBC)` or `sda(-0x4FC0)`).
/// - `out_glyph`: receives the result of `0x801AFDB0(flag, code)`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Two stores through the out pointers; the decoder helpers only read.
///
/// # Safety
/// `text` must point at a readable character; the UTF-8 decoders require a
/// terminator within their scan window. Both out pointers must be writable.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - the mode ladder, the two lead/trail ranges and the two font bases
/// are literal. `// inferred:` `mode` is also the allocator's encoding
/// argument, because the export reuses the same register (`iVar7`) for both
/// and only overwrites it with `1` inside the remap branch.
