/// kind from `0x801CF4B0` (kind `2` and a zero status from `0x801B4560` keep
/// kind `1`), commits them with `0x801B4680`/`0x801B7470`, tears down both
/// caches, and then asks the disc layer whether the reset is allowed:
/// `0x801D6230` (disc present) runs the first block, `0x801ABF20(0xE0, 0x20)`
/// the second. Both blocks end in the same debug prints because a failed reset
/// returns. Finally the power block is zeroed with `0x800046B4`, the reset
/// record is read by `0x801D64A0`, decoded by `0x801B82F0` on kind `1`, and the
/// menu state is committed through `0x801B3410(5)`.
