/// Evaluates the keyframe tracks of one record into a `0x40`-byte block.
///
/// The low half of `0x802DCD64` is the output block and the high half the
/// record context. The sample time `t` is clamped to
/// `[sda2(-0x4AA8), u16(context+4 -> record)[+0x34]]`; the clamped value picks
/// the animation frame bit in the record's frame table, and the unclamped value
/// is handed to the track samplers. Every float track is either a literal at
/// `context + field` (when its flag bit is set) or a self-relative offset to a
/// `0x8023F000` key table at `context + field + offset`. The output layout is
/// `{+0 flags, +4 mask, +8 x, +0xC y, +0x10 z, +0x14..+0x1C extra,
/// +0x20 colour, +0x24..+0x2C variant fields, +0x30..+0x34 variant-2 fields,
/// +0x38 colour, +0x3C track}`.
///
/// # Original
/// - Removed: the modelled `_savegpr_23` prologue call (`0x802DCD64`) and the `_restgpr_23` epilogue call (`0x802DCDB0`).
///   The save `bl` returns no value; the value it appeared to return is the incoming `r3`/`r4` register pair.
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80241eb0` at `0x80241eb0` (1000 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80241eb0_FUN_80241eb0.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `t`: sample time. The export keeps it in `f1` (`extraout_f1`) and prints
///   the entry as `void`, so it is an undeclared floating-point argument.
/// - `_arg0`, `_arg1`: the incoming `r3`/`r4` handoff pair, the context and the
///   size out-pointer.
///   the entry as `void`, so it is an undeclared floating-point argument.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing; the block comes from `0x802DCD64` and is released to `0x802DCDB0`.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Between eight and sixteen word stores plus one sampler call per track.
///
/// # Safety
