/// - `child`: second word compared against `+0x2888`.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing.
///
/// # Side effects
/// At most one virtual `0x10003` notification, one `+0x2888` clear, or one
/// `0x80257FC0` child walk.
///
/// # Safety
/// `object` must be live; when `object + 0x2888` matches `child` that pointer
/// must carry a callable `+0x0C` slot.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the shift mask, the `0..8` bound, the `0x10001` test, the `0x10003`
/// id and both branches are literal; the original has no null test before the
/// `+0x2888` compare, and neither does this body.
